{"availability":"available","full":"yacobwood/BTCC","name":"BTCC","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2025-09-06T16:03:36Z","updated":"2026-10-12T23:04:14Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://btcc-ten.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://btcc-ten.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T23:51:26.305Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T23:51:26.305Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T23:51:26.305Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T23:42:59.379Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T15:05:59.138Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-12T23:51:26.305Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This is the authoritative technical reference for the BTCC Hub mobile application. It covers the product, architecture, data pipeline, backend services and operational processes end to end."],"features":["Applies last-known cached flags from AsyncStorage instantly (no network block)","Fetches fresh flags with an 8-second timeout, then applies global flags + per-device overrides","Per-device overrides are keyed by FCM token inside the overrides object in flags.json and are never cached.","The most complex store. Manages all user notification preferences and FCM topic subscriptions.","Every setSetting() call triggers syncAllTopics(), which subscribes or unsubscribes from each FCM topic based on the full PARENTCHAIN hierarchy. A leaf topic is only subscribed when its own value AND all parent values…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yacobwood/BTCC/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c5ef6bd84c69f34fe8d6c27dd38de74da6b15d3a993a15e18f3f69017228e952","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:27.244Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T23:51:26.503Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This is the authoritative technical reference for the BTCC Hub mobile application. It covers the product, architecture, data pipeline, backend services and operational processes end to end.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yacobwood/BTCC/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"No donation link (2026-10-12): the Android-only \"Buy me a coffee\" card, its donor name prompt and the chat supporter badge were removed after Google Play rejected the app under its Payments policy (donations to a non-tax-exempt developer must use Play billing or not exist).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yacobwood/BTCC/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Bans are stored at /chat/bans/{authorId} (authorId = the sender's Firebase Auth uid - anonymous sign-in gives every install one on first launch, see store/auth.js; this stays stable across a rename and even across later linking a Google/Apple account, since linking keeps the same uid).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yacobwood/BTCC/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Cross-device sync (Firestore user profile): a setting only survives a reinstall/new device/re-login if its key is listed in both SYNCEDKEYS here (gates whether setSetting() calls saveProfile()) and PROFILEASYNCKEYS in userProfile.js (gates uploadLocalProfile()/applyProfileToStorage(), both invoked from auth.js's onAuthStateChanged).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yacobwood/BTCC/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"That meant every btcc.net-facing workflow had to share one single self-hosted runner (label btcc-mac, a launchd service on the maintainer's own Mac).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yacobwood/BTCC/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"Every btcc.net-facing scraper (scrapenews.py, scrapearticles.py, scrapecalendar.py/scrapefulltimetable.py, scrapeteamstats.py, scrapebtccstats.py, scrapegallery.py, and finally scrapecircuitimages.py) now fetches via Scrapfly's paid Scrape API (tools/scraper/scrapflyfallback.py's fetchviascrapfly/fetchimageviascrapfly/fetchimagesmart) instead of local Playwright - asp=true…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yacobwood/BTCC/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"required","text":"Every scraper workflow auto-retries once before alerting (added 2026-09-01 for the 5 btcc.net-facing workflows, originally to cut noise from self-hosted-runner contention, kept after the Scrapfly migration since a transient Scrapfly/parse blip deserves the same treatment; extended 2026-09-06 to race-day-start.yml, scrape-penalties.yml and scrape-youtube.yml, which previously…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yacobwood/BTCC/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"c5ef6bd84c69f34fe8d6c27dd38de74da6b15d3a993a15e18f3f69017228e952","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yacobwood/BTCC/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T23:51:26.507Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-12T23:04:14Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yacobwood/BTCC/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T23:51:26.525Z","hash":"c5ef6bd84c69f34fe8d6c27dd38de74da6b15d3a993a15e18f3f69017228e952","originalBytes":315515,"storedBytes":315515,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["own","every","same","only","race","one","live","driver","src","article","rather","via","data","real","results","app","round","each","image","session","page","already","when","never","now","car","before","both","since","scrape","which","notification","still","team","see","fixed","lap","tab","confirmed","new","run","after","fetch","just","any","once","two","btcc.net","grid","added","instead","name","screens","day","had","per","used","user","above","first","admin","news","year","photo","chat","file","actually","full","screen","state","device","json","number","articles","their","android","minutes","other","title","card","ever","hub","qualifying","read","directly","gallery","points","button","content","failure","github","shows","api","drivers","store","url","back","fallback","retry",